{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>When Chedorlaomer came.</b> Scripture tells of the might of this king together with the kings who were with him, that they struck down the mighty men who dwelt in cities of strength and fortress — this is בעשתרות קרנים, for the strength of the beast is its horns. And they also struck down those who were the wealthy of the people along with their multitudes — this is ואת הזוזים בהם. And Scripture teaches you that since they struck the Rephaim, who are the mighty men, within fortified cities, it is unnecessary to mention the mighty men who were in the plain — this is ואת האימים אשר בשוה קריתים. The Emim are the mighty ones who cast terror (אימה); בשוה קריתים means in the cities of the plain. And there is no need to mention those who worked the land who were in a fortified place on their mountain, which is Seir — this is ואת החורי בהררם שעיר. And it is known that the Horites were workers of the land, and so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: why are they called Horites (חורי)? Because they sniff the earth like a snake (כחויא). And the meaning of עין משפט is the rock in Kadesh, in which Moses is destined to be judged. And the meaning of בחצצן תמר is 'in the inner part (חציון) of Tamar' — that is, the land of Israel, which is in the midst of the world, where the Amorite dwells. And Scripture elaborated in narrating this war and the great might of Chedorlaomer and the kings who were with him, who defeated the kings along with the great mighty men dwelling in fortress cities and along with their great multitudes, in order that from this the matter of Abraham our father be publicized — that in his great might he defeated the kings who had been victorious, as it says afterward: אחרי שובו מהכות את כדרלעומר ואת המלכים אשר אתו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:20.460726655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}